        "original_id": "5c487761-69bf-5741-8575-675277dce849",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Terry Ray, Michael York, Mickey Rooney, Dean Jones, Rhonda Fleming, Peter Patzak, Peter Maffay, Tahnee Welch, Armin Mueller-Stahl, Elliott Gould, Massimo Ghini\n- Places: Dorothy Chandler Pavilion\n- Works: Hollywood Goes Classical, Lethal Obsession\n- Topics: acting, writing, film, stage performance\n\nFacts:\n- Michael York was born Michael Hugh Johnson on 27 March 1942 and is an English actor.\n- Terry Ray’s first professional writing job was the stage performance \"Hollywood Goes Classical\" at the Dorothy Chandler Pavilion.\n- \"Hollywood Goes Classical\" starred Mickey Rooney, Michael York, Dean Jones, Rhonda Fleming, and other classic film stars.\n- \"Lethal Obsession\" is a 1987 German crime-thriller film.\n- Peter Patzak wrote and directed \"Lethal Obsession.\"\n- \"Lethal Obsession,\" also known by the German title \"Der Joker\" and as \"The Joker,\" starred Peter Maffay, Tahnee Welch, Michael York, Armin Mueller-Stahl, Elliott Gould, and Massimo Ghini.",
